<title>USA: Cyclone over southern New Caledonia - WSC.</title>
<headline>Cyclone over southern New Caledonia - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Drena is over southern New Caledonia, moving southeast with top winds of 105 mph, private forecaster Weather Services Corporation (WSC) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Damaging winds and flooding rains are occurring, but should taper off as the storm accelerates into the waters southeast of the islands, weakening and turning extratropical within 48 hours.</p>
